CRIME NARRATIVE ARC — 18-BEAT STRUCTURE
No headings in script output
================================================================================

 1.  Cold open — discovery / last moment / impossible claim / forensic tease
 2.  Case label + stakes line ("यह सिर्फ हत्या नहीं थी...")
 3.  Story promise — "इस वीडियो में हम बताएंगे..."
 4.  VICTIM HUMANIZATION — who they were, what they loved, what they worked for
     [CRITICAL: before any crime detail appears]
 5.  Relationship setup — how victim and perpetrator were connected
 6.  THE SURFACE LIFE — how everything appeared normal / happy from outside
 7.  THE CRACK — first sign something was wrong (behavior / digital / money)
 8.  THE HIDDEN WORLD — perpetrator's secret (affair / debt / resentment / plan)
 9.  THE DECEPTION COVER — how the killer built their false alibi / cover story
10.  OBJECT / FORENSIC HOOK appears — the one thing that quietly breaks the lie
     [second biggest surprise — must land between minutes 4–8]
11.  INVESTIGATION BUILD — CDR / DNA / CCTV / postmortem / digital recovery
     [each step as a dramatic scene with visual anchor]
12.  KILLER AT PEAK — cover story working, public sympathizing, killer confident
     [this is villain's best moment — must be in second half]
13.  THE PIVOT — the one detail that collapses the cover story
14.  INTERROGATION CRACK — the exact moment the prepared story breaks
15.  CONFESSION / ARREST — kept procedurally accurate but cinematically paced
16.  SYSTEMIC ANGLE — what institution / system / loophole made this possible
     (social media trust / child marriage / corporate HR failure / VIP access /
      police inaction / evidence tampering / foreign funding)
17.  VICTIM TRIBUTE — not just the crime but what was lost
18.  Reflection + comment question + Like/Subscribe CTA + धन्यवाद / जय हिंद

